### Step 1: Total number of cows before adding new ones

Each of the 10 stalls has 20 cows:

$$
10 \text{ stalls} \times 20 \text{ cows per stall} = 200 \text{ cows}
$$

---

### Step 2: Mr. Sylas buys 40 cows and divides them **equally among the 20 stalls**

So he adds **40 cows** to **20 stalls**, meaning:

$$
\frac{40 \text{ cows}}{20 \text{ stalls}} = 2 \text{ cows per stall}
$$

So now, each of the **20 stalls** has:

$$
20 \text{ original cows} + 2 \text{ new cows} = 22 \text{ cows per stall}
$$

---

### Step 3: How many cows are in **8 of the stalls**?

Each of the 8 stalls has 22 cows:

$$
8 \text{ stalls} \times 22 \text{ cows per stall} = 176 \text{ cows}
$$

